WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.178
When Alex opened a bank account, the bank checked who they were.

2
00:00:04.178 --> 00:00:09.023
Now Alex wants a credit card from another company, which must run its own checks.

3
00:00:09.873 --> 00:00:15.541
Usually that means the same passport, the same proof of address, and another copy of both.

4
00:00:16.392 --> 00:00:22.449
Alex asks the bank for a statement of what it verified: which checks, by what method, and when.

5
00:00:22.449 --> 00:00:26.147
The statement is signed, and holds no images of documents.

6
00:00:26.147 --> 00:00:27.677
It goes into Alex's pod.

7
00:00:28.526 --> 00:00:33.515
The card company offers a choice: fill in the form, or use a verified identity.

8
00:00:34.365 --> 00:00:37.950
Alex grants it one record, to be read once, within the hour.

9
00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:40.400
It is the narrowest grant in these demos.

10
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:51.464
The card company reads the statement and checks three things: the signature, that the statement has not been withdrawn, and that the bank is on its list of issuers it has an agreement with.

11
00:00:52.314 --> 00:00:53.748
That agreement matters.

12
00:00:53.748 --> 00:01:00.543
One institution may rely on another's checks only under conditions, and the list stands for those conditions.

13
00:01:01.393 --> 00:01:06.984
The card company did not see the identity document, the bank account, or anything else in the pod.

14
00:01:07.835 --> 00:01:10.400
If it asks again, the pod refuses.

15
00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.511
A one-time grant is used up.

16
00:01:13.361 --> 00:01:15.999
Later, Alex loses the identity document.

17
00:01:16.849 --> 00:01:20.017
The bank withdraws its statement and issues a new one.

18
00:01:20.017 --> 00:01:24.007
Anyone checking the old statement will see that it no longer stands.

19
00:01:24.857 --> 00:01:27.782
One set of checks, two institutions, one read.

20
00:01:27.782 --> 00:01:34.078
And two ways to take something back: the owner withdraws access, and the issuer withdraws its word.

21
00:01:34.929 --> 00:01:41.851
To work on reusable identity with other EDMA members, join the Solid Community of Practice.
